The unix accounts the objects of this namespace may run rootless containers
as, by name or by uid.

A rootless container runs as the account its rootless_user keyword names. The
account owns the container, its images and its files, and whoever runs a
container as it reaches everything else it owns on the node, the rootless
containers of other objects included. So the accounts are listed here, where
only the squatter writes, and a namespace administrator setting rootless_user
to an account not listed is refused. The primary group of a listed account is
allowed too.

An account allowed in two namespaces lets each reach the containers of the
other. It is allowed, and warned about.

Root is not bound by the list, and the root account is never allowed, whatever
it says. Empty, the default, allows no account.
